# Task Completion Workflow

After finishing **every** implementation task, always do these two steps before reporting done — no exceptions:

## 1. Update Documentation

Update all three docs to reflect the completed work:

- **`docs/LiveKitVoiceAgentPlan.md`** — mark the item done (strikethrough row, ~~status~~, annotation with date + files changed), update the sequencing section, update any feature-status tables.
- **`docs/LiveKitVoiceAgentREADME.md`** — update the feature status table (§9a.11 or equivalent) and any relevant sections (call flow, troubleshooting, quickstart).
- If the task introduced a significant new subsystem, add a troubleshooting entry.

## 2. Add Tests

Add tests alongside the code — not as a separate task later:

- **Unit tests**: new logic (pure functions, condition matching, state machines) → `tests/unit/` in the relevant service.
- **Integration tests**: new API endpoints, DB mutations, worker load paths → `tests/integration/` or `tests/test_*.py`.
- Follow existing test file naming (`test_<module>.py`) and fixture patterns in the repo.
- Tests must pass before the task is reported complete (`make test-unit` or equivalent).
- A feature the plan marks as done must have at least one test asserting the thing it does — a form that writes a row no test reads is the pattern we are explicitly avoiding.

## Checklist (run mentally before saying "done")

- [ ] Plan doc updated — item struck through with date
- [ ] README feature status updated
- [ ] New tests written and passing
- [ ] No linter errors on modified files (ReadLints)
